  "content": {
    "id": "p27-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "The population of a country is increasing exponentially at a rate of $4\\%$ per year. Determine how long it will take for the population to double, correct to the nearest year.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "18 years",
      "worked": "Let $P_0$ be the initial population and $t$ the time in years. The annual growth multiplier is $1.04$, so $P(t)=P_0(1.04)^t$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P_0(1.04)^t &= 2P_0\\\\(1.04)^t &= 2\\\\t\\log_{10}(1.04) &= \\log_{10}2\\\\t &= \\frac{\\log_{10}2}{\\log_{10}(1.04)}\\\\t &\\approx 17.67299\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe population doubles after approximately 18 years, to the nearest year.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 48
  },
